1
00:00:00,175 --> 00:00:02,265
Your county can't fix what it can't see.

2
00:00:02,895 --> 00:00:03,823
No ride.

3
00:00:04,553 --> 00:00:07,002
A clinic that closes before your shift ends.

4
00:00:07,732 --> 00:00:09,267
Forms too hard to read.

5
00:00:09,997 --> 00:00:11,228
A six-week wait.

6
00:00:11,958 --> 00:00:13,732
No one who speaks your language.

7
00:00:14,412 --> 00:00:16,109
We count the people who show up.

8
00:00:16,489 --> 00:00:18,113
Not the ones who never made it.

9
00:00:19,193 --> 00:00:23,936
Six in ten local health departments serve fewer than 50,000 people.

10
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:26,265
Small teams. Big jobs.

11
00:00:27,245 --> 00:00:30,760
CB-CAP shows where care breaks, so you know what to fix first.

12
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,407
See where people drop off on the way to care.

13
00:00:35,587 --> 00:00:37,874
See which barriers stop them, by neighborhood.

14
00:00:39,454 --> 00:00:42,490
Small numbers stay hidden. Privacy comes first.

15
00:00:43,866 --> 00:00:45,904
Every number shows where it came from.

16
00:00:47,184 --> 00:00:49,459
AI writes the first draft of your report.

17
00:00:49,889 --> 00:00:53,217
It never sees private data. It never makes up numbers.

18
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:56,290
A person checks every word before it goes out.

19
00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:01,320
Built for health equity, rural health, and small teams doing more.

20
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,303
Walk into your budget meeting with real numbers.

21
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:10,308
Bring CB-CAP to your county. Talk to the SozoRock Foundation.

22
00:01:11,088 --> 00:01:12,831
Care. For every zip code.
